1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Moses Mordechaj ROTHENBURG, Chief Rabbi. Rabbi in Tykoczin, Brest Litovesk, chief rabbi of Altona. Born o. 1665. Died Jan. 11. 1712 in Altona. D. Jan. 12. 1712 in Königstrasse. ~ M. VII.65 Rechle FÜRST (-1752). See
2 CONC  sect. 1.2. Rabbi first in Tykoczin, then in Brest Litovesk and finally in Altona. The last place he shared rabbinate with Zebi Hirsch Ashkenazi (also called Hakam Zebi, possibly his brother). Since this left Altona in 1710, Moses
2 CONC  was Rothenborg chief rabbi. This lasted only a little over one year since he died 12 January 1712. Talmudic records of him and his father Mordechai R. Susskind was released by the widow Rechle f. Fürst in the book "Scháloth Utesc
2 CONC huboth". Her cousin rabbinatsassessor Joseph Fürst (sd) wrote the preface, and the publication was financed by the rich Goldschmidt family (Josef Fürst maternal lineage), presumably led by Royal. Hofagent Bendix Goldschmidt (sd). 
2 CONC The book was published Hamburg in 1716 (sometimes listed incorrectly Amsterdam 1746). http://tom.brondsted.dk/genextracts/?ancline&chpt=1&ged=2&sid=I10
