2 CONT
2 CONT *[http://www.encyclopedia.com/religion/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/lichtenstadt-abraham-aaron   Encyclopedia.com]: LICHTENSTADT, ABRAHAM AARON (d. 1702), *Court Jew and primator ("leader") of the Bohemian Landesjud
2 CONC enschaft. '''Lichtenstadt''' has been identified with [https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbi-Aharon-Schlackenwerth/6000000014232238020 '''Aaron Schlackenwerth'''] (d. 1694) and also with '''Abraham Aaron''' of Frankfurt, but '''Tobias
2 CONC  *Jakobovits''' established that he was the son of the physician '''Naphtali Hirz Oettingen''' of Przemysl (Poland). He took his family name from his place of residence, Hroznetin (Lichtenstadt). First mentioned as agent of the co
2 CONC urt of Saxony, he became the shtadlan of Bohemian Jewry in 1673. In 1680 he persuaded *Leopold i to cancel the order expelling the Jews from the Planá community (see *Chodová Planá), and later secured for the Jews the right to att
2 CONC end the Leipzig fairs. He was instrumental in having '''Abraham *Broda''' appointed as chief rabbi (Landesrabbiner) of Bohemian Jewry in 1689. As a result of internal strife in the Jewish community, he was denounced for abusing hi
2 CONC s position when determining the allotment of taxes. Legal proceedings were opened in 1692, and although a case could not be established against him, Leopold i removed him from his post and had him, his son '''Solomon''', and the s
2 CONC ecretary (Landschreiber) of the Landesjudenschaft imprisoned. The complicated trial which followed was one of the most prominent of its kind at the time. In 1693 he was released from prison and restored to office in 1701; those wh
2 CONC o had denounced him were imprisoned.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Die Inschriften des alten Judenfriedhofes in Wien bei dr. Bernhard Wachstein- 1 teil- , page 449
