2 CONC Manuscripts Collapse Author/Creator: London, Hermann Date: 1885. Imprint: Berlin, Content and Scope: Manuscript containing the genealogy of Hermann London's family. A note indicates that Abraham Michalski transcribed this version 
2 CONC from a handwritten manuscript. Family members were rabbis in Lublin, Brisk, Nikolsburg, Krakau, Frankfurt an der Oder, Prenzlau, and London. Some biographical notes concerning Hermann London are included. Historical Notes: Hermann
2 CONC  London was the chairman (Vorstehender) of the Adass Jisroel congregation in Berlin, died 1899. Subject: Rabbis: Germany. Geographic: Berlin (Germany) Corporate: Adass Jisroel (Berlin, Germany) Rights: This material may be used fo
