1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Moses Behrendt ROTHENBORG, grocery. Grocery store in Copenhagen. Born in 1735 in Hamburg-Altona. Death 10 November 1787 in Copenhagen. D. Nov. 12. 1787 in Møllegade. ~ August 26. 1771 in Copenhagen mV17 Regina (Ros
2 CONC e, Rosalie)? (1745-1804). - See below. Must have come to Copenhagen as about 4-year-old in 1739. Termed merchant and merchant, but little is known about his business. In 1771 he co-signatory of the congregation funeral protocol, t
2 CONC hus considered as one of the church leaders.
2 CONT
2 CONT pic "Moses, son of Ber Rothenburg".
2 CONT
2 CONT In road maps from 1777 and the census in 1787 indicated he to stay in Kompagnistræde 58 Snarens Neighborhood. The grocery business still seems to be in no. 50, at her father's original address. He died November 10, 1787, buried in
2 CONC  Møllegade. Sources [1], [14] (p. 171) mm.
2 CONT
2 CONT pic Moses, Ben Ber Rothenburg's tombstone in Møllegade. "Here is the honest man Mr. Moshe son of the late leader Mr. Ber Rojtenberg, great-granddaughter and grandson of the famous Gaon (erudite) of Rojtenberg [ie Rabbi of Lublin M
2 CONC ordechaj Suskind R., see above]. Dead Saturday and was buried Sunday morning after the first day of Kislev year 5548th May his soul ... "and so on. http://tom.brondsted.dk/genextracts/?ancline&chpt=1&ged=2&sid=I10
1 FAMC @F6000000027238813467@
1 FAMS @F6000000027239467085@
1 RFN geni:6000000027239509937
