1 NAME R' Aharon HaKohen Jampoller
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1821
1 TITL R'
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In a Yichus paper drafted by https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbi-Dr-J-Simcha-Cohen/6000000002702955788, based in on the work of his grandfather, https://www.geni.com/people/R-Samuel-Burstyn-A-B-D-Shatowa-from-1887/60
2 CONC 00000031963085073, as well as his own research, R' Simcha Cohen describes his descent from https://www.geni.com/people/R-Aharon-HaKohen-Jampoller/3096983. In the notes about this ancestor is written: "R' Aharon was considered a ko
2 CONC han M'Yuchas, direct descendant from Rabba and the father-in-law of R. Levi Yitzchok, Berdichiver, author of 'K'dushat Levi' "
2 CONT
2 CONT The Rabba referred to here is Rabbah b. Nahmani, https://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/articles/12485-rabbah-b-nahmani, a Kohain who lived circa 270- circa 330 CE and was Rosh Pumbedita for the last 23 years of his life, according to
2 CONC  the Jewish Encyclopedia. Since Rabbah b. Nahmani is considered to be a descendant of Eli (upon consultation with genealogist R' Shraga Kahana), therefore this R' Aharon HaKohen of Jampoller is theoretically a descendant of the It
2 CONC hamar-Eli line from Aharon rather than the Eleazar line from Aharon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Utsr HaRabanim: #1600
