2 CONT
2 CONT Chief Rabbi of Glogau for most of his life and in his final years served as Ashkenazi Av Beit Din of Amsterdam. He wrote a Haskama for the Pnei Moshe, by R’ Moshe Katz ABD Mezhibuzh and Przemysl.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Haskama for the Pnei Moshe is dated Sunday the second day of Shevat 5476 which is January 26, 1716. So he definitely was alive in 1716.
2 CONT [https://hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=6332&st=&pgnum=3 Link to the Haskama]
