1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rabbi and Talmudist in Glogau (Glogow) and later Breslau (Wroclaw).  Scion of the famous rabbinical Caro family from Glogau according to the testimony of https://www.geni.com/people/R-Yitzchak-Rappaport-ABD-of-Liss
2 CONC a/6000000002765045831
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the research of Paul J. Jacobi, Rabbi Naftali Caro, called "Gloger", was Dayan in Glogow, and fathered R' Hirsch Caro of Rawitsch. According to Jacobi, Rabbi Naftali was the son of Rabbi Yisrael Caro ABD of Flatow (so
2 CONC n of Rabbi Isak Selig Caro ABD Hanover). But according to Rabbi Naftali's tombstone inscription (in Breslau) his father's name was Rabbi Dov Baer Caro. It seems Rabbi Dov Baer Caro was a brother of Rabbi Yisrael Caro ABD of Flatow
2 CONC  and they were both sons of Rabbi Isak Selig Caro ABD Hanover.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Possibly identical with https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbi-Naftali-Caro/6000000077553001951.
2 CONT According to the research of Paul J. Jacobi, a Rabbi Naftali Caro, called "Gloger", was Dayan in Glogow, and fathered R' Hirsch Caro of Rawitsch. According to Jacobi, Rabbi Naftali was the son of Rabbi Yisrael Caro ABD of Flatow (
2 CONC son of Rabbi Isak Selig Caro ABD Hanover). But according to Rabbi Naftali's tombstone inscription (in Breslau) his father's name was Rabbi Dov Baer Caro. It seems Rabbi Dov Baer Caro was a brother of Rabbi Yisrael Caro ABD of Flat
2 CONC ow and they were both sons of Rabbi Isak Selig Caro ABD Hanover.
