1 OCCU writer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.encyclopedia.com/religion/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/caro-david
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.virtualjudaica.com/Listing/Details/1425663/Techunath-Harabanim-David-ben-Yechiel-Caro-Lemberg-1879
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Caro
2 CONT
2 CONT from Jerwish Encyclopedia: CARO, DAVID: By: Louis Ginzberg, S. Mannheimer
2 CONT
2 CONT Prussian pedagogue; born about 1782 at Fordon, grand duchy of Posen; died Dec. 25, 1839, at Posen. He belonged to the school of the Meassefim, and devoted his great literary talents to the enlightenment of his brethren, to the ref
2 CONC orm of Judaism, and to the cultivation of the Hebrew language. Under the pseudonym "Amittai ben Abida Aḥiẓedeḳ" he defended the Hamburg Reform Temple in "Berit Emit" (Covenant of Truth, Dessau ["Constantinople" on title-page], 182
2 CONC 0), the first part of which, "Berit Elohim" (Covenant of God), was published by the author himself, and the second part, "Berit ha-Kehunnah" (Covenant of the Priesthood), or "Tekunnat ha-Rabbanim" (Character of the Rabbis), by Jud
2 CONC ah Löb Mieses of Lemberg. A new edition of the second part, with additions by Mieses, was published at Lemberg in 1879.
2 CONT
2 CONT Many of Caro's articles, essays, and poems appeared in "Ha-Meassef" and in the "Bikkure ha-'Ittim." He was a prolific writer, and left a number of manuscripts on literary, lexicographical, bibliographical, and pedagogical subjects
2 CONC . Among his inedited works are a Hebrew translation of Zunz's "Gottesdienstliche Vorträge der Juden," with notes and additions; a Hebrew translation of the same author's biography of Rashi, with notes; and biographies of celebrate
2 CONC d rabbis. Bibliography:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Ha-Meassef, viii. 33; ix. (4), 14, 63; x. (1), 25, 44; (2) 26, 56, 88:
2 CONT     Bikkure ha-'Ittim, xi. 58, 61, 66, 168, 180, 182, 183, 184;
2 CONT     Allg. Zeit. des Jud. iv. 615 et seq., v. 48, 49;
2 CONT     N. Lippmann, Leben und Wirken des David Caro, Glogau, 1840;
2 CONT     Zunz, in Asher's Benjamin of Tudela, ii. 300;
2 CONT     Grätz, Gesch. der Juden, xi. 425, 426;
2 CONT     Steinschneider, Cat. Bodl., col. 816;
2 CONT     idem, Hebr. Bibl. xxi. 45.
