1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Philip Moses ROTHENBORG, thehandler. The- & porcelain act in Copenhagen. Birth 22 December 1783 in Copenhagen (Mos). Died in 1840 in Copenhagen. D. June 30, 1840 in Møllegade. ~ May 31, 1808 in Copenhagen (Mos) m. 
2 CONC IV.9 Frederikke ADLER (1793-1827). See sect. 1.5. Citizenship o Copenhagen 1810. Had the business originally in the Queen Tværgade 342 (directory 1814/15 "Thehandler, Committee of Borlys and Soap"), but established since one Tea a
2 CONC nd porcelain trade in Købmagergade, which later became "Salmon's tea shop." In directory for 1817-18 found him living on Spring Street (later Pilestræde) 31 in Copenhagen. In 1836 directory contrast Gl.Mønt 101 - close to his sons
2 CONC  David Philips and Peter Philips residence. Died June 30, 1840 in Copenhagen after nearly 13 years as a widower. http://tom.brondsted.dk/genextracts/?ancline&chpt=1&ged=2&sid=I10
