2 CONC en an energetic woman; his son Natan Feitel (d. 1609) was rabbinical assessor in Prague...; his son Weidl (Veit Munk the Younger) was a rabbi in Worms and Vienna, where he died in 1630; his son Simon died in 1650; and his daughter
2 CONC s were Bathsheba, Rosel, Nechama, and Vogele."
