1 NAME Uri Shraga Pheibish Pheibish Eliezer /Chalfan/ ABD Brod
2 GIVN Uri Shraga Pheibish Pheibish Eliezer
2 SURN Chalfan
2 NSFX ABD Brod
2 _MARNM Maneles
2 NICK Phöbus
2 NICK Feiwel
2 NICK Feiwisch
1 NAME אורי שרגא פייביש /פרענקל מב"ח ה"דת אש"/
2 GIVN אורי שרגא פייביש
2 SURN פרענקל מב"ח ה"דת אש"
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1660
2 PLAC Vienna
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Austria
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1707
2 ADDR
3 CITY Prague
3 STAE Prague
3 CTRY Czechia
1 OCCU
1 TITL Rabbi
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 132 
2 CONT
2 CONT Uri Schragga Feibish (Veibish) bn Elieser m’beit Chalfan, dajan No Year (Footnote: see Letzte Vertreibung) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maneles Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT haGaon mvhr"r Feibisch AB"D dk"k Broda bn Eleazar Maneles Brod z"l  1706/07  Gal-Ed #87, which mentions his dau. Sarah e' David Koref 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://zayt.org/collections/pragapublica/4822?p=265
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In the introduction to a book he published in 1806, Rabbi Yitschak Frenkel from Huncovce mentions his great-grandfather Shraga Feibish Frankel, who was a rabbi in Uherský Brod (Moravia). It is unknown whether he used the family na
2 CONC me Frankel in his interaction with non-Jews. Rabbi “Uri Schraga Phöbus b. Elieser Chalfan” served as rabbi of Ungarisch-Brod in 1700-1708 (Kalman Nürnberger, “Geschichte der Juden in Ung. Brod,” in Hugo Gold (ed.), Die Juden und J
2 CONC udengemeinden Mährens in Vergangenheit und Gegenwart: ein Sammelwerk (Brünn: Jüd. Buch- u. Kunstverl., 1929), 549–559). In 1692 Rabbi "Uri Shraga Pheibish, the son of Eliezer from the house of Chalfan" signed the notules of the bu
2 CONC rial society of Prague (Simon Hock, Die Familien Prags: Nach den Epitaphien des alten jüdischen Friedhofs in Prag (Prague: A. Alkalay, 1892), 132). His book Sefer Dat Esh was published posthumously in Berlin in 1743 by his son Mo
2 CONC she Yosef. Moshe Yosef wrote an introduction that mentions an additional son called Eliezer, who was dayan in Prague. The introduction of the author mentions his father Eliezer from Vienna.
