1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Leser dajan bn haRav haGaon Feibish Lichtenstadt z”l darschan b’Prag, AB”D dk”k Brod v’Bumsla  1745/46
2 CONT
2 CONT 194	Leser dajan peh Prag z”l bn haRav haGaon Feibisch Lichtenstadt z”l darschan b’Prag, AB”D v’R”M dk”k Broda v’Bumsla 1746 (Footnote: See my book Wiener Exulanten pg. 182)194	
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT He explains why it took so long to publish his father’s book. It was because “my brother the great darshan (=someone who gives a sermon) and dayan (=rabbinical judge) in the holy community of Prague Rabbi Eliezer …. prevented [it]
2 CONC ”.
2 CONT
2 CONT 	Leßer Feisch Lichtenstatt	Prag	6 Hrn Ambt	1 Occupation: Brand Silber
2 CONT
2 CONT Family members:
2 CONT                 Ehefrau Fraidl
2 CONT                 Sohn Faisch
2 CONT                 Tochter Rachel
2 CONT                 Tochter Chaye
2 CONT
2 CONT Household members:
2 CONT                 Dwora v. Raudnitz - Bediente ledigen Stands
2 CONT                 Nachem außen Elßas - Studenten oder Kostgänger
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT In the introduction to a book he published in 1806, Rabbi Yitschak Frenkel from Huncovce mentions his grandfather Eliezer (=Lazar). In the introduction Moshe Yosef wrote to his father's book Sefer Dat Esh, which was published in B
2 CONC erlin in 1743, he mentioned his brother Eliezer, who was dayan in Prague. 
