2 _MARNM Appelbaum
1 NAME Kurt Appelbaum
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 9 DEC 1904
2 ADDR
3 CITY Berlin
3 STAE Berlin
3 CTRY Germany
1 DEAT
2 DATE 29 JAN 1990
2 ADDR
3 CITY New York
3 STAE New York
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Pianist
1 TITL Dr.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Kurt Appelbaum''' was a concert pianist who fled the Nazis for the United States in 1938, after the Anchluss of Germany and Austria. He was a student of Artur Schnabel. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Kurt Appelbaum, Pianist, 84, Published: February 1, 1990
2 CONT
2 CONT Kurt Appelbaum, a pianist and teacher, died of a heart attack on Monday at St. Luke's Hospital. He was 84 years old and lived in Manhattan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Appelbaum was born in Berlin and began playing the piano at the age of 4. He studied with the renowned German pianist Artur Schnabel, and made his debut in Berlin in 1930.
2 CONT
2 CONT The pianist immigrated to New York in 1939, one year after a successful debut at Town Hall. He had an active concert career, specializing in the works of Beethoven and Schubert. In the late 1940's he began recording the 32 Beethov
2 CONC en Sonatas for Westminster Records, but the project was left incomplete when the company went out of business.
2 CONT "United States Social Security Death Index," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:JBR7-747 : 7 January 2021), Kurt A Appelbaum, 29 Jan 1990; citing U.S. Social Security Administration, Death Master File,
2 CONC  database (Alexandria, Virginia: National Technical Information Service, ongoing).
2 CONT
2 CONT He had taught privately for the last 25 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are no immediate survivors.
