2 CONT
2 CONT The date of birth does not seem correct. He was "son #8" which meant he was born two children after Rabbi Yaakov Israel Emden (who was born in 1697). Also, given that numerous other siblings were born after Nathan, it does not mak
2 CONC e sense that he was born the year his father died. A more logical estimation of his death would be 1701, which would have made him 97 when he died in 1798 (unless his death date is also in error), or unless the order of birth is a
2 CONC lso incorrect.
