1 NOTE {geni:about_me} According to the book "Zichron Yehuda", Lvov, 1894, p. 6a, Rabbi Naphtali Hirz Broda, Rabbi of Mykulyntsi (Mikulińce), Ukraine was the son of Rabbi Aaron Broda of Kalvarija, https://www.geni.com/people/Aaron-Broide
2 CONC -A-B-D-Kalwarija-and-later-dayan-Vilnius/6000000004588057180
2 CONT On the other hand, in the Book Nitei Neemanah, Jerusalem, 1909, p. 37, it is claimed that Naphtali was named Broda becaus he came from Brody, Ukraine, but that he had no connection with the Broda family. This corresponds with the 
2 CONC version shown here in Geni. This information should be treated with some suspicion. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source :Book Review: Meorei Galicia (Encyclopedia of Galician Sages) Jerusalem, Israel, 1978-1997. Author: Rabbi Meir Wunder. Reviewed by Chaim Freedman 
2 CONT
2 CONT He {Aryeh Leib Auerbach} had a son Rabbi David Tzvi and daughters: Reizel the wife of Rabbi Meshullam Zalmen Ashkenazy ABD Pomeran, and when he died at the age of 25 she married Rabbi Tsvi Hersh Margolis ABD Lublin (and some say R
2 CONC abbi Betzalel Margolis ABD Ostroah, and there is a third opinion); the wife of Rabbi Naftali Herz Broda ABD Mikolinitz; the wife of Rabbi Khaim ABD Slopkowitz son of Reb Uri of Zolkiew; and there are those who say also the wife of
2 CONC  Rabbi Nakhman of Horodenka.
