1 NOTE {geni:about_me} G14.5 R. Aryeh Leib (Leon) Album from the Hebrew letters of Aryeh Leib Ben Isaac Mendel = Album, originally Rabinowitz, born in Zeimys in 1872 and died in Philadelphia on March 27, 1960...... he was internationally
2 CONC  known as the author of the newspaper column "My Notebook" which appeared in the ''Philadelphia Jewish Exponent,'' ''Elimira Sunday Telegram'', ''The San Francisco Emanuel'', and other national newspapers.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served in Philadelphia as Rabbi at the Congregation  ''Shaari Zedek'', and then at Congregation ''Bnai Zvi'' until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source
