1 NAME Joseph (Yoef) Saul (Shaul) /Rabinowitz/
2 GIVN Joseph (Yoef) Saul (Shaul)
2 SURN Rabinowitz
2 _MARNM Rabinowitz
2 NICK Reb Yosef Shaul
1 NAME Rabbi Joseph Saul Rabinowitz
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Moshassuck Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Central Falls
3 STAE Rhode Island
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1840
2 ADDR
3 CITY Krekenava
3 STAE Panevėžys County
3 CTRY Lithuania
1 DEAT
2 DATE 26 OCT 1893
2 ADDR
3 CITY Providence
3 STAE Rhode Island
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joseph Saul was the grandson of the renowned Reb Shlaima from Zeimelis (Zheimel).   He became an esteemed Torah scholar in his own right and was probably a student of his father's.
2 CONT
2 CONT Little is known about his early life.  He lived in Krakanova and married Leah Beila (also known as Beila, her family name is unknown). They produced at least 8 children (it is said there may have been more). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Leah Beila was the businesswoman and was in all likelyhood, the main family provider, at first. She must have been good at it - they had servants in the home. Joseph Saul looked after the children in those early years. He studied 
2 CONC Torah most of the time and became a learned man in the community which produced many learned men.  
2 CONT
2 CONT However, he had 5 daughters for whom he had to provide dowries, so in about 1888 he went to the U.S.A. to seek his fortune and the records show that in 1891 he was a pedlar working in and around Providence in Rhode Island.  
2 CONT
2 CONT In that year Joseph Saul and his cousin Rabbi Nathan Yehudah Leib Rabinowitz organised Chevrot Shas Umishnah attached to the Sons of Zion (Bnei Zion) congregation then established in Providence. The congregation included a Jewish 
2 CONC Communal Centre incorporating amongst others a daily Talmud Torah as well as an Adult education (Bible studies) programme. The educational programme followed the concept of brotherliness, of praying together,  sharing meals and vi
2 CONC siting, particularly the sick. The group organised by Joseph Saul and his cousin emerged from that educational programme.
2 CONT
2 CONT Unfortunately Joseph Saul did not live to see the Chevrot grow. In 1893 at the Chanukat Habayit (opening/inauguration) of the synagogue, the building of which he inspired, he apparently gave a fiery droshah (sermon), caught pneumo
2 CONC nia and died.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was buried at Moshassuck Cemetery in Providence, Rhode Island, in a specially constructed tomb and vault. Today only the front marker, the tombstone, still stands. There is a hole in the centre of the tombstone indicating that 
2 CONC it was riveted onto the vault.
2 CONT
2 CONT The legend on the monument (translated from the Hebrew by Rabbi William G Braude of Providence) reads as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT 	The very stone cries out of the wall 	Joseph is no longer 	He left alas this life, 	Returned before he grew old, 	He went to heaven 	But his spirit still lives in our midst. 	And his deeds will ever bring him to rememberance. 	Ea
2 CONC ch will work to make his presence known	 	From afar to live here his feet brought him	 	
2 CONT 	Whenever his brethren sought him in the house of G-d they found him 	There he taught Torah, spreading knowledge, drawing after him twin camps, 	Morning and evening, out of his abundant knowledge of Torah he taught talmud 	and Mis
2 CONC hnah. 	In the presence of companies of men he set forth the lore of the twins of gazelle. 	At the sound of his voice men gathered  and held council upon the Foundation 	stone. 	How great are his deeds, his glory and his constancy.
2 CONC  	May his memory be a blessing and his reward be very great. 	He is the distinguished scholar, descendant of a noble family, scion of martyrs 	our master Yoseph Shoel, son of Rabbi Hayim Rabinovitz, whose memory is a 	blessing, of
2 CONC  the City of Krakinova. 	He went to his eternal rest on the sixteenth day of Mar-Chesvan in 5654, in the 	reckoning of centuries.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reb Joseph Saul Rabinowitz was highly respected in the community, a 'descendant of a noble family, scion of martyrs". For a number of years after Joseph Saul's death congregants of the Ben Zion community would gather at  his tomb 
2 CONC on the anniversary of his death to study Torah.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Leah Beile was left to care for the large family by herself - the girls not yet married when Joseph Saul died.  Solly Frank remembers her - he says she was a remarkable woman.  She managed to keep her sons out of the Tzars army, s
2 CONC ending two of them out of the country - Jankel to the U.S.A. (he later went to South Africa) and Leib (Louis) to South Africa. She found husbands for all her daughters.  It is said that "when Leah came into shul all the women stoo
2 CONC d up". 
2 CONT
2 CONT Leah died of natural causes - old age - in Bakhmach in Russia in 1917, where she had gone with her daughter Bella Devorah Frank and her family to escape the advancing German army.
2 CONT
2 CONT The first born of each of her grandchildren was named after her husband Joseph Saul - Shiela Kriger, Joe Green, Saul Frank, Joe Cohen. In memory of Leah there are many Leahs, Lily's,  Leilas.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Source Emmy Maisel, Judy Hansen, the Rhode Island Jewish Historical Assoc.]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT He is buried in the Mohassuck cemetary, 978 Lonsdale Ave, Central Falls, RI 02863-1719; Ph: 401-723-1087     and we are related to Shaul Vaal through him.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Rhode Island Jewish Historical Association (rijha.org) has info on him in their annual journal, "Rhode Island Jewish Historical Notes" on pages 249-250, 254, and 274; as well as his info on his cousin, Rabbi Noson Yehuda (Nath
2 CONC an L.) Rabinovitz on pages 4:241, 244-245, 247, 249, 257, 269, 271, 274; 7:413; 11:384. Rabbi Noson Yehuda Leib Rabinovitz was the chief rabbi of Providence (and previously a Dayan in Slobodka) and wrote a sefer called Yad Yehuda 
2 CONC (published 1897). Here is a link to it http://www.hebrewbooks.org/2958 . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional Info: Rabbi Yosef Shaul was the descendant of the well known Rabbi Shaul Vaal Katzenellenbogen, known for his being the King for a Day in Poland and annuling decrees against Polish Jewry of the time. He in turn was a de
2 CONC scendant of the well known Rabbi Meir Katzenelenbogen, who was known as the Maharam of Padua. Family legend has it that he also descended from Rabbi Moshe Isserles, commonly known as the "Remah", author of the Ashkenazic "Shulchan
2 CONC  Aruch", the Jewish Code of Law
2 CONT --------------------
