1 OBJE
2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p14/91/e1/c3/7f/5344486126a7f367/jozef_osias_rubin_and_malka_keyla_horowitz_-_marriage_record_-_9_mar_1837_original.jpg?hash=38d50fac38387d996da58223a81c28e57fcf448fad9c1856442ab3d918581468.1794988799
2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Jozef Osias Rubin and Malka Keyla Horowitz - Marriage Record - 9 Mar 1837
2 NOTE Akta #12.
3 CONT
3 CONT Translation: In the year 1837, on the 9th of the month of March, at noon. This happened in gmina/comune 10 of the free city of Kraków in house at # 109 and 10 [109 and 110 I suppose] where we came upon the request of the parties. 
3 CONC Before us, Wojciech Kucieński, Civil Registrar in the free city of Kraków established for the Jews in gmina/commune 2 residing, personally appeared Jew Józef Osias Rubin, bachelor, having completed his 17th year of age, according 
3 CONC to extracted birth certificate from the Kahal books of the city of Tarnów in Galicia Imperial Austria (alegat #1), son of Hirsch Rubin, merchant in Galicia Imperial Austria in city Tarnów residing, and Channa Cyrla Rubin(owa), his
3 CONC  wife already deceased, as presented in official certificate from the Tarnów city council issued on 27 February this year (alegat #2), in Galicia Imperial Austria in city Tarnów with his father residing, for the performance of thi
3 CONC s act, they came to Kraków and temporarily in the house where act took place staying, with respect given to his father and father's permission to marry (alegat #3), on the one side. Appeared also Jewess Małka Kejla, two names, Hor
3 CONC owitz, unmarried woman, having completed her 21st year of age, according to extract of her birth from the civil records of Kraków (alegat #4), daughter of Beniamin Horowitz, money-changer, and Maria nee Goldess, spouses, residing 
3 CONC in the house where the marriage taking place, with her parents living and with their assistance working, on the other side. The parties facing the signifier license of the ruling senate the city of free Kraków and its district to 
3 CONC conclude this marriage in the local country, on 27 January this year #302 (#5) [I guess permission needed because groom from Galicia]
3 CONT continuing in summary...
3 CONT Banns: announcements on behalf of groom in synagogue city Tarnów (alegat #6); announcements on behalf of bride in her home gmina/commune, in Kraków at #176 Kanonicza street, first on the 12th and second on the 19th of February thi
3 CONC s year
3 CONT Witnesses: Szymon Nachiatz?, merchant, Wolf Feldmann, baker, Izrael Lachner, day-laborer, and Izaak Fest/Fert?, journeyman merchant, residing on Kanonicza in Kraków
