1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *[http://www.geni.com/people/Mrs-Joshua-Leib-HaLevi-Heschel/6000000007641335648#/tab/media  '''Family Tree] Isaac A.B.D. Brody, Brzezany  ("Saul Wahl" by Dr. Neil Rosenstein, page 273) 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Many of his descendants adopted the name of "Babad,  (B.A.B.A.D.  -  sons of the Av Beth Din)''.
2 CONT
2 CONT אבי שושלת באב"ד
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT From the Encyclopedia Judaica (2007):
2 CONT
2 CONT BABAD, a family of rabbis. The founder of the family was Isaac of Cracow, son of Issachar Berish, a parnas of the Council of Four Lands, and grandson of Heschel, av bet din of Cracow. He served as rabbi of Brzezany and then of Bro
2 CONC dy, where he died in 1704. His children added the word Babad (an acronym of Benei Av Bet Din, ``children of the av bet din´´) to their signatures, and it eventually became their surname.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------
2 CONT "BABAD" = sons of the Av Beth Din.
2 CONT
2 CONT His children are referred to in state records by the name of RABINOWITZ. [Yivo Encyclopedia of Jews in Eastern Europe]
