1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hinda PERLA, daughter of Boruch, the Levy
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the stone, she died in late 1822. The cemetery is said to have opened that year, so this may be the oldest burial there.
2 CONT
2 CONT This is most likely Hinda PERLA, daughter of Boruch, wife of Wigdor (Avigdor), who died in Lomza in late 1822 at age 78, leaving six sons and one daughter. [Lomza Deaths for 1821/22, Number 204.]
2 CONT
2 CONT The inscription has been translated as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT We go forth in weeping [unknown word]
2 CONT
2 CONT Weeping over the death of our mother
2 CONT
2 CONT A woman of valor, modest
2 CONT
2 CONT and prominent. Hinda
2 CONT
2 CONT the daughter of Baruch HaLevi, who passed away
2 CONT
2 CONT On the eve of the Sabbath, 5 Cheshvan
2 CONT
2 CONT 5583 [1822]
2 CONT
2 CONT May her soul be bound in the bonds of eternal life
