1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Julius was born in Rouxville, S Africa, but was educated to be a lawyer in Berlin.  Because of his birth he was able to rescue his family and in-laws from the Nazi regime and return to S Africa in 1938. He fought i
2 CONC n WW1 on the German side and received a number of shrapnel wounds. Before WW2 he was living with his family at W15 Joachinstaler Strasse 37. He was asked to return to Germany after the war as a judge, but he declined. He is descen
2 CONC ded from a dynasty of rabbis, through his paternal grandmother,  see ‘ The Unbroken Chain’
