1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT Translation from Russian
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Roman Semyonovich Pines''' Born on 08.10.1885, Moscow; b/n; zavod "Forward" head of the group of orders and sales.. Lived: Leningrad, pr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arrested 8 March 1935
2 CONT
2 CONT Sentenced: OS NKVD USSR March 11, 1935, obv.: SOE.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sentence: Exile to Kazakhstan for 5 years Rehabilitated on August 31, 1989. Prosecutor's Office of Leningrad
2 CONT
2 CONT ~ Source: Archive of the Research Center "Memorial" (St. Petersburg)
2 CONT
2 CONT ~ [http://lists.memo.ru/index.htm Victims of political terror in the USSR, 4th edition] 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Translation from the Russian:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Roman Semyonovich Pines''' (1895-1938) - was born in Moscow; after the family moved to St. Petersburg, he studied at the real department of Petrishula from 1895 to 1903. At the time of his arrest, he worked as the head of the ord
2 CONC ers and sales department at the Vperyod foundry and mechanical plant in Leningrad. Lived at the address: Nevsky pr. 29, kv.3. Nationality: Jewish; partisanship: b / n; social affiliation: employee.
2 CONT
2 CONT First arrest: March 8, 1935. Sentenced: OS NKVD USSR March 11, 1935; charge: ESR (socially dangerous element). Sentence: exile to 5 years in Kazakhstan. In 1937 he lived in the city of Kuibyshev.
2 CONT
2 CONT Second arrest: October 25, 1937; Sentenced: "troika" at the UNKVD in the Kuibyshev region on December 31, 1937; charged under Art. 58-10 and Art. 58-11; Sentence: to 10 years in a correctional camp. Died in 1938.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the first sentence, he was rehabilitated in 1989 by the Prosecutor's Office of Leningrad; on the second sentence, he was rehabilitated on December 3, 1956 by the Kuibyshev Regional Court.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Source: Book of memory of the Samara region.
2 CONT
2 CONT ~ [http://lists.memo.ru/index.htm Victims of political terror in the USSR, 4th edition] 
