1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See [http://toladot.blogspot.co.uk/2014/03/blog-post_24.html this] Hebrew blog for the source that https://www.geni.com/people/R-Avigdor-Karo-A-B-D-Leslau-and-Pinsk/6000000022410970351 had a son called Chaim. Note,
2 CONC  there is no '''conclusive''' evidence to prove this.
2 CONT
2 CONT Chaim the son of Avigdor of Pinsk authored [http://aleph.nli.org.il:80/F/?func=direct&doc_number=000043652&local_base=NNLMSS this book], still in manuscript.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Lebendiger/Lebendiker family tradition, they are descended from https://www.geni.com/people/R-Avigdor-Karo-A-B-D-Leslau-and-Pinsk/6000000022410970351. It follows therefore that this Chaim is likely "Chaim Lebendik
2 CONC er son of Avigdor" in 1816 Karolin, Pinsk district, Minsk Gubernia Revision List (see photo uploaded) -- Joshua Levin (March 17, 2018). There are a few records missing to make the actual connection though.
2 CONT
2 CONT The surname Lebendiger is probably an adaption of Haimowitz (lit. son of Chaim), a name often recorded for https://www.geni.com/people/R-Avigdor-Karo-A-B-D-Leslau-and-Pinsk/6000000022410970351. See [https://dbs.bh.org.il/he/%D7%9C
2 CONC %D7%91%D7%A0%D7%93%D7%99%D7%92%D7%A8/%D7%A9%D7%9D%D7%9E%D7%A9%D7%A4%D7%97%D7%94 this] article for a possible theory.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the above-mentioned 1816 revision list entry, we see only one son listed, Ela Ekhiel (born 1800) married to Leya. It is unclear whether this is a father, brother, or uncle to https://www.geni.com/people/Moshe-Moses-Lebendiger/6
2 CONC 000000003327792328. Ela Ekhiel may possibly be the translation of Eliyahu Yehezkel. https://www.geni.com/people/Moshe-Moses-Lebendiger/6000000003327792328 had a son https://www.geni.com/people/Yechezkel-Charles-Lebendiger/60000000
2 CONC 03682131923 - who according to his gravestone was actually called Eliahu Yechezkel! Another son of https://www.geni.com/people/Moshe-Moses-Lebendiger/6000000003327792328 was called https://www.geni.com/people/Haim-Lebendiger/60000
2 CONC 00004099713846.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the above-mentioned revision list, Chaim's wife was called Hindla.
