1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Source===
2 CONT
2 CONT According to [http://www.rishonim.org.il/petach-tikva/info/founder_show.aspx?id=109 this] article, the father of the grandfather of https://www.geni.com/people/R-Simcha-Israelit/6000000000862191263 was https://www.geni.com/people/
2 CONC R-Avigdor-Karo-A-B-D-Leslau-and-Pinsk/6000000022410970351.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/R-Simcha-Israelit/6000000000862191263 's father https://www.geni.com/people/Avigdor-Israelit/6000000075593057948 was presumably named after https://www.geni.com/people/R-Avigdor-Karo-A-B-D-Leslau-and-Pi
2 CONC nsk/6000000022410970351.
2 CONT The problem is that https://www.geni.com/people/Avigdor-Israelit/6000000075593057948 's father father was not called Avigdor. Neither was https://www.geni.com/people/Avigdor-Israelit/6000000075593057948 's mother's father.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT The most likely solution is that the article is referring to https://www.geni.com/people/Avigdor-Israelit/6000000075593057948 's grandfather's father. Since the identity of https://www.geni.com/people/Avigdor-Israelit/600000007559
2 CONC 3057948 's father's father's father is known, this must be a reference to https://www.geni.com/people/Avigdor-Israelit/6000000075593057948 's mother's father's father. https://www.geni.com/people/Avigdor-Israelit/60000000755930579
2 CONC 48 's mother's father is recorded as 'Simcha' on his daughter Freidel's record.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT An alternative conclusion could be that it is indeed a reference to https://www.geni.com/people/R-Simcha-Israelit/6000000000862191263 's grandfather's father; not through his father Avigdor but through his mother. That, that https
2 CONC ://www.geni.com/people/Avigdor-Israelit/6000000075593057948 was called Avigdor is a coincidence, it was his wife who was descended not he. <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT If one adopts this conclusion https://www.geni.com/people/Mordechai/6000000075602762380, was https://www.geni.com/people/R-Avigdor-Karo-A-B-D-Leslau-and-Pinsk/6000000022410970351 's son and not this Simcha.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT However, besides for the unlikely coincidence of them sharing the same name, particularly since Avigdor is not such a common name, it appears from the way the writer in the above-linked article contrasts https://www.geni.com/peopl
2 CONC e/R-Avigdor-Karo-A-B-D-Leslau-and-Pinsk/6000000022410970351 with https://www.geni.com/people/Avigdor-Israelit/6000000075593057948 - the former being a Mitnaged and the latter becoming a Chassid - that it was https://www.geni.com/p
2 CONC eople/Avigdor-Israelit/6000000075593057948 himself who was the descendant not his wife.
