1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rebbe Raphael, was a hidden tzadik. He lived in a village near Parzeczew. He operated a tavern in the townlet and dealt with the gentry, but he was a great servant of God. Hasidim told that this innkeeper was a tru
2 CONC ly holy man. Rebbe Raphael – so hasidic tales tell - once traveled all alone with his wagon on the road. Suddenly several armed robbers sprang out of the forest, with outstretched swords. The robbers did not want to satisfy themse
2 CONC lves only with the money that Rebbe Raphael offered them. They wanted to kill him also. At that moment a horseman came along, in the form of a military man. As soon as the robbers saw him, they quickly ran away. But at the same ti
2 CONC me the rider also vanished. Rebbe Raphael was sure that this horseman who saved his life was Eliyahu Hanavi (Elijah the Prophet).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
